Focus on mid to large enterprise companies (250 - 5000+ employees) headquartered in Switzerland
Take on additional responsibility within the team, identify and take ownership and drive projects that bring value to the wider business:
Generate new clients for our outstanding travel and spend technology
Own the entire sales process from the first touchpoint, present product demos to potential clients, negotiate and do the follow-up until closing the deal;
Understand the needs of our target prospects and articulate the value that Perk provides. Follow the entire sales cycle;
Stay up-to-date with new features and product launches;
Help define and establish best practices together with the broader team;
Monitor and report on sales performance analytics and forecasts;
Mastering to consult conservative clients into digital opportunities;
Owning the conversations between C level stakeholders in finance, procurement, IT, and travel management;
Evaluate the existing infrastructure of the clients and consult the individual SaaS solutions;
Suggest innovative upsell / partner ideas to increase sales and improve customer experience.

Being a native German speaker and fluent in English is a must;
Fluency in French is a plus
Possess excellent communication, presentation, and public speaking skills;
Be hungry and ambitious, yet ethical and sound;
Be able to work as an individual contributor, but remember you are part of a team;
Be a customer-centric mindset.

* Supporting implementation and managing business and IT projects in the area of HR, with a focus on transformations around digital HR;
* Managing programs and projects in both national and international environments;
* Conceptual design of HR and HR IT strategies, as well as HR target operating models in the context of HR cloud implementations;
* Supporting and implementing organizational, process-related, IT-related and personnel change initiatives in the HR organization;
* Managing and planning training measures to facilitate change adoption;
* Efficiently linking processes between business, strategy and IT to ensure cohesive and effective transformation initiatives;
* Engaging in impactful work within a leading global management consulting environment standing for integrity and global mindset, with flexibility across client sites, Capgemini offices, and remote work.

* Master-s degree from a recognized University in the field of Economics, Social Sciences, or Information Technology;
* At least 3 years of practical project experience in the field of digital transformation in at least one of the following industries: Insurance, Consumer Goods and Retail, Manufacturing or Life Science;
* Practical experience in project management (minimum partial) in the HR environments, with comprehensive knowledge of HR strategy, organization, processes;
* Rational thinking and ease of combining technological understanding, strategic evaluation, and implementation work i.e., efficient linking of processes between business, strategy, and IT;
* A structured reliable work style with a fun approach to solving complex tasks with eagerness to learn and adapt in uncertain situations and manage multiple tasks simultaneously with a commitment and self-responsibility toward deadlines;
* Strong communication and presentation skills in English and German are mandatory on the C1 level minimum;
* Very good MS Office skills.

